    "sources": [
      "MAME src/mame/sega/naomi.cpp @59e7c0b INPUT_PORTS 'naomi' (generic \u2014 no dedicated wldkicks port map; game list lines 11132-11141)",
      "MAME src/mame/sega/naomi.cpp @59e7c0b game-list comment lines 11140-11141 (wldkickspj/wldkickspw): \"'PCB' means upright version, uses analog button on control panel to kick the ball\" \u2014 Namco itself shipped the kick as an analog button",
      "Flycast fork core/hw/naomi/naomi_roms_input.h lines 577-613: wldkicks_inputs = per-player STICK L/R + U/D analog axes 0-7, one BUTTON, plus per-player analog KICK channel on axes 8-11; wldkickspcb_inputs = CHANGE button + stick + 'BALL' Half axis (RT)",
      "Flycast fork core/hw/maple/maple_jvs.cpp: class jvs_namco_v226 (line 1092, 12 analog channels) dispatched on gameId \"WORLD KICKS\" (line 1569) \u2014 KICK axes 8-11 read mapleInputState[p].halfAxes[PJTI_R], i.e. the DC pad's analog right trigger; settings.input.fourPlayerGames = true; jvs_namco_v226_pcb (line 1170) derives the upright's 6 'Ball button' bits from the same trigger",
      "https://www.highwaygames.com/arcade-machines/world-kicks-6168/ \u2014 World Kicks SD cabinet: analog joystick for movement/aim + per-player physical soccer ball 'mounted to the bottom of the cabinet ... which reacts to the strength of the player's kick'; 4 players per cabinet, 'Link 2 cabinets together for 8 players'",
      "Game's own attract 'How to control' screens: assessments/evidence/wldkicks/shot-121s.png + shot-548s.png \u2014 stick diagram plus foot-kicking-ball diagram ('Your character will tackle when you kick the ball on defence', 'Shoot!')"
    ]
